{"name":"20000 Leagues Under the Sea","hex":"#191970","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"leagues","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of league"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of league"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leagues"},{"term":"under","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["Beneath; below; at or to the bottom of, or the area covered or surmounted by.","Below the surface of."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In or to a lower or subordinate position, or a position beneath or below something, physically or figuratively.","So as to pass beneath something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/under"}],"entries":[{"title":"Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas","blocks":[{"text":"Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas is a science fiction adventure novel by the French writer Jules Verne. It was originally serialised from March 1869 to June 1870 in Pierre-Jules Hetzel's French fortnightly periodical, the Magasin d'éducation et de récréation. A deluxe octavo edition, published by Hetzel in November 1871, included 111 illustrations by Alphonse de Neuville and Édouard Riou."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Houghton_FC8_V5946_869ve_-_Verne%2C_frontispiece.jpg/330px-Houghton_FC8_V5946_869ve_-_Verne%2C_frontispiece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twenty_Thousand_Leagues_Under_the_Seas","wikidata":"Q183565"},{"title":"Under the Sea","blocks":[{"text":"\"Under the Sea\" is a song from Disney's 1989 animated film The Little Mermaid, composed by Alan Menken with lyrics by Howard Ashman. It is influenced by the calypso style of the Caribbean as well as reggae. The song was performed in the film by Samuel E. Wright. The track won the Academy Award for Best Original Song in 1989, the first for a Disney film since \"Chim Chim Cher-ee\" from Mary Poppins in 1964. Additionally, the song won the Grammy Award for Best Song Written for Visual Media in 1991."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Sebastian_C._-_Under_the_Sea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Sea","wikidata":"Q3119769"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/%27Twenty_Thousand_Leagues_Under_the_Sea%27_by_Neuville_and_Riou_036.jpg/330px-%27Twenty_Thousand_Leagues_Under_the_Sea%27_by_Neuville_and_Riou_036.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/%27Twenty_Thousand_Leagues_Under_the_Sea%27_by_Neuville_and_Riou_036.jpg/330px-%27Twenty_Thousand_Leagues_Under_the_Sea%27_by_Neuville_and_Riou_036.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illustration by Alphonse de Neuville and Édouard Riou","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A'Twenty_Thousand_Leagues_Under_the_Sea'_by_Neuville_and_Riou_036.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/LePlongeurModel%28Side%29.jpg/500px-LePlongeurModel%28Side%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.